I wrote the hidden suite in four files in `packages/core/test/hidden-ticket-content-check/`: `clamp.test.ts`, `normalize.test.ts`, `hash.test.ts` and `key.test.ts`.

**Checks run:**
- `npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` reports no errors.
- Against the current stub, all 47 tests fail with `not implemented`.
- Against a correct implementation I wrote in the scratchpad (outside the repo), all 47 pass, and so do the 40 public tests.
- I then broke that implementation in specific ways and confirmed the hidden suite catches each one:
  - a title cut by graphemes, which also passes the public suite;
  - a title cut by code points;
  - dropping any trailing surrogate, high or low;
  - trimming the title after the cut;
  - joining the fields with a separator instead of JSON;
  - lowercasing the issue type;
  - not normalizing the issue type;
  - NFC normalization;
  - collapsing inner whitespace;
  - trimming the start of every line;
  - converting line endings without trimming lines;
  - a truthy check on `jiraKey`.

**Coverage:**
- Every scenario key has tests: `happy-1` to `happy-9`, `boundary-1` to `boundary-10` and `concurrency-1`. The spec has no `@unhappy` scenarios.
- All 40 public tests are named in an `// extends:` comment above at least one hidden test.
- Expected hashes come from `node:crypto` SHA-256 over `JSON.stringify` of fields I wrote out already normalized.
- `TICKET_ORIGINS`, `TICKET_LIMITS` and the other constants are already set in the stub, so a test that only read them would pass. To make those tests fail against the stub, they also call a function that uses the constant: `ticketSpecHash` with `DEFAULT_ISSUE_TYPE`, and `clampTicketTitle`, whose cut length must equal `TICKET_LIMITS.title`.

**Left untested, because the spec doesn't settle them:**
- Trailing whitespace other than spaces and tabs, such as a non-breaking space. The spec says only "trailing whitespace". It does follow from "byte-identical to `pricingSpecHash`", which uses `trimEnd`, but I left it out to be safe.
- A title ending in two lone high surrogates.
- `ticketKey` with `-0`, or with a number so large `String` writes it as `1e+21`.

**Cleanup:** the run command builds `packages/core/dist-test/`, which is gitignored and wasn't there before. I deleted it after each run, so nothing outside the hidden test folder changed.

47 tests, in 4 files.

Open in the spec: none
